     {
      "label": "job",
      "head": "Oil does *four* jobs",
      "pose": "present",
      "face": "smile",
      "prop": {
       "type": "tags",
       "items": [
        "LUBRICATE",
        "COOL",
        "CLEAN",
        "SEAL"
       ]
      }
     },
     "It lubricates moving parts, carries away heat, traps dirt, and helps seal the pistons."
    ],
    [
     "c16_3",
     {
      "label": "pump",
      "head": "A *pump* keeps it flowing",
      "pose": "count",
      "face": "grin",
      "prop": {
       "type": "oilsys"
      }
     },
     "An oil pump pushes oil from the sump up to the crankshaft, camshafts and turbo."
    ],
    [
     "c16_4",
     {
      "label": "wear",
      "head": "Oil *wears out*",
      "pose": "shrug",
      "face": "smug",
      "prop": {
       "type": "oilsys",
       "dirty": true
      }
     },
     "Over time, oil breaks down and fills with dirt, so it protects less and less."
    ],
    [
